<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY'S MKB TO CUT PRIME RATE 1/2 PT TO 21 PCT.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY'S MKB TO CUT PRIME RATE 1/2 PT TO 21 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Magyar Kulkereskedelmi Bank Rt (MKB Rt) said on Tuesday it would reduce its prime lending rates on forint loans to 21 percent, from the current 21.50 percent, effective August 15.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
